{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>HaShem you have declared this day.</b> When you undertook to enter the covenant under the oath of imprecation, in which every material good is lost if you transgress it, you declared and exalted the blessed El thereby — so that fulfilling His will is more honored in your eyes than any material good." "<b>To be to you for Elohim.</b> That He be, in your eyes, the separate being honored above all separate entities, and that from Him comes all the governance and sustenance of your affairs without any intermediary, as is fitting for that which is eternal — so that it is fitting for you to serve and submit to Him alone, as is fitting for the Supreme and your Guide, and to pray to Him, since He alone is your Guide." "<b>And to walk in His ways.</b> To resemble the most honored of all other existent beings." "<b>And to hear His voice.</b> As is fitting for His servants."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:19.162807455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}